+        <span class="t">A figure eight is a path you can walk without stopping. That is the club's actual mechanics: the weekly circuit, the repeat booking, the habit that closes on itself. The shape describes the behaviour the business sells.</span>
+      </div>
+      <div class="mean rv" data-d="3">
+        <div class="mean__top"><span class="mean__n"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-eight"/></svg></span>
+          <span><span class="mean__k">Reading 03</span><b>The numeral</b></span></div>
+        <span class="t">Eight is two full circles stacked: balance, completion, eight hours of sleep, and half the world's lucky number. A name with a numeral also hands the system a counting device for later. Rituals, rooms and blocks can carry it.</span>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+    <div class="card card--ink rv" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
+      <span class="klabel"><svg class="ico"><use href="#i-eye"/></svg> A note from our own method</span>
+      <p class="body" style="margin-top:.55rem">We usually insist a mark comes out of the product, not out of a word trick. age8 bends that rule: the gesture lives in the glyph. What saves it is that the loop is also physically true. The training circuit <strong>is</strong> a closed path, so the shape points at the floor, not only at the typography. That is the argument to test, not to assume.</p>
